<v Katy Shanahan>And they just sort of crossed their hands and went with the impasse. Which was fairly astounding because you know, a court order is nothing to scoff off. It's the highest court in our state demanding that you redraw a map. And the commissioners just said-- yeah, no, we're not gonna do that. And had no qualms about not only doing that, but then filing paperwork with the court to explain-- yeah, we're just not gonna follow your court order.
<v Katy Shanahan>他们只是交叉双臂，选择了僵局。这相当令人震惊，因为你知道，法院命令是不容忽视的。这是我们州最高法院要求你重新绘制地图。而委员们只是说——是的，不，我们不会那样做。而且不仅这样做，随后还向法院提交文件解释——是的，我们只是不会遵守你的法院命令，这毫无愧疚。

00:33:05.520 --> 00:33:16.230
<v Katy Shanahan>And of the five Republican commissioners, four of them are barred attorneys who swear an oath to uphold the constitution of the United States and of Ohio, and to have respect and deference to courts who have jurisdiction over your actions, and that's how you're going to behave, you're just gonna cross your arms and say, yeah, no, I'm not gonna comply with that that court order. It's appalling.
